Former Secretary of State Brad Johnson and businessman Mark Perea ran for the Republican nomination,<ref name=ewhitney>{{cite news|last1=Whitney|first1=Eric|title=Brad Johnson Explains Why He's Running For Governor Of Montana|url=http://mtpr.org/post/brad-johnson-explains-why-hes-running-governor-montana|access-date=September 29, 2015|publisher=Montana Public Radio|date=September 28, 2015}}</ref> but were defeated by businessman [[Greg Gianforte]]. [[Attorney General of Montana|Montana Attorney General]] [[Tim Fox (politician)|Tim Fox]] had been speculated as a potential candidate, but instead chose to run for re-election.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bozemandailychronicle.com/news/politics/ag-tim-fox-files-paperwork-for-re-election-in/article_f16024e0-6b98-11e4-b30f-8f66281cf801.html|title=AG Tim Fox files paperwork for re-election in 2016|publisher=The Bozeman Daily Chronicle |date=November 13, 2014 |access-date=November 15, 2014}}</ref>

Bullock won re-election, taking 50.2% of the vote. Gianforte won 46.4% of the vote.<ref name="politicoresults"/>

