{{Main|2016 Washington gubernatorial election}}
One-term incumbent [[Governor of Washington|Governor]] [[Jay Inslee]] ran for re-election. Inslee was elected in [[2012 Washington gubernatorial election|2012]] with 51.4% of the vote against [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] [[Attorney General of Washington|Attorney General]] [[Rob McKenna]]. Inslee previously served as a U.S. Representative from 1993 to 1995 and from 1999 to 2012. [[Seattle]] Port Commissioner Bill Bryant<ref name=what2014>{{cite news|last=Connelly|first=Joe|title=What 2014 elections say about 2016 governor's race|url=http://blog.seattlepi.com/seattlepolitics/2014/09/29/what-will-2014-elections-tell-us-about-our-2016-governors-race/|access-date=October 2, 2014|newspaper=[[Seattle Post-Intelligencer|Seattlepi]]|date=September 29, 2014|archive-date=October 6, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141006110152/http://blog.seattlepi.com/seattlepolitics/2014/09/29/what-will-2014-elections-tell-us-about-our-2016-governors-race/|url-status=dead}}</ref> advanced to the November general election. Potential Republican candidates include U.S. Representatives [[Jaime Herrera Beutler]] and [[Cathy McMorris Rodgers]], State Senator [[Michael Baumgartner]], and former State Representative [[Cathy Dahlquist]].<ref name=what2014 /><ref name=McKenna>{{cite news|last=Rosenthal|first=Brian|title=Former AG McKenna joins law firm|url=http://www.yakimaherald.com/news/yhr/wednesday/854831-8/former-ag-mckenna-joins-law-firm|access-date=March 4, 2013|newspaper=Yakia Herald|date=February 19, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130928074803/http://www.yakimaherald.com/news/yhr/wednesday/854831-8/former-ag-mckenna-joins-law-firm|archive-date=September 28, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=Cornfield|first=Jerry|title=If not McKenna, others could challenge Inslee in 2016|url=http://www.heraldnet.com/article/20130606/NEWS01/706069918|access-date=July 10, 2014|newspaper=[[The Herald (Everett)|HeraldNet]]|date=June 6, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714220708/http://www.heraldnet.com/article/20130606/NEWS01/706069918|archive-date=July 14, 2014|url-status=dead|df=mdy-all}}</ref>

Inslee won re-election, taking 54.2% of the vote. Bryant won 45.5%.<ref name=Data/>

