{{Main|2016 Puerto Rico gubernatorial election}}
One-term incumbent [[Governor of Puerto Rico|Governor]] [[Alejandro García Padilla]] was eligible to run for re-election, but chose to retire.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://news.yahoo.com/puerto-rico-governor-not-seek-reelection-232840409.html|title=Puerto Rico governor will not seek reelection|publisher=Yahoo| date=December 15, 2015 |access-date=December 15, 2015}}</ref> García Padilla is a member of the [[Popular Democratic Party of Puerto Rico|Popular Democratic Party]] (PDP).<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.caribbeanbusinesspr.com/news03.php?nt_id=75736&ct_id=1 |title=Fortuño: Romney would be good for PR |newspaper=[[Caribbean Business]] |date=August 28, 2012 |access-date=January 15, 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130925190410/http://www.caribbeanbusinesspr.com/news03.php?nt_id=75736&ct_id=1 |archive-date=September 25, 2013 |url-status=usurped |df=mdy-all }}</ref>

[[David Bernier]], former [[Secretary of State of Puerto Rico]] and former President of the [[Puerto Rico Olympic Committee]], won the PDP nomination for governor.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://in.reuters.com/article/usa-puertorico-election-idINKBN0TY2JO20151216|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151222092547/http://in.reuters.com/article/usa-puertorico-election-idINKBN0TY2JO20151216|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 22, 2015|title=Bernier plans to announce Puerto Rico governor bid Wednesday|publisher=Reuters|author=Brown, Nick | date=December 16, 2015 |access-date=December 16, 2015}}</ref>

[[Resident Commissioner of Puerto Rico]] [[Pedro Pierluisi]], who is affiliated with the [[New Progressive Party of Puerto Rico|New Progressive Party]] (PNP).<ref name=PierlusiGov>{{cite news|last=Gonzalez|first=Rocio|title=Unlike Puerto Rico governor, Pedro Pierluisi has four more years|url=http://www.voxxi.com/puerto-rico-pedro-pierluisi-four-years/|access-date=March 4, 2013|newspaper=Voxx|date=November 12, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130926100706/http://www.voxxi.com/puerto-rico-pedro-pierluisi-four-years/|archive-date=September 26, 2013|url-status=dead|df=mdy-all}}</ref> and activist and political commentator [[Ricky Rosselló]] sought the PNP nomination for governor, and Rosselló won the nomination.

Rosselló won the election.

